  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a strong multimodal anchor to calibrate the search. config_021 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) combines a well-established RNA encoder (scvi_n200), a powerful image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), the more informative multiprofile setting, an expressive transformer aggregation, and a simple/robust concat fusion. This tests the core hypothesis that multimodal fusion with strong per-modality encoders yields high accuracy, while keeping the fusion strategy simple to isolate encoder and aggregation contributions. It provides a high-quality reference point: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can exploit by swapping individual components (e.g., scgpt, weighted fusion); if it underperforms, we learn which component to simplify. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the 10-experiment budget."
}

